      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum ibuprofen dose for adults.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The limit is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use without supervision.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** The limit is usually 800 mg per dose. 1,600 mg in one dose adds GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular risk without any added benefit.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders are:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
     ],
